WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:44.378
Do you want to go get tteokbokki?

00:44.462 --> 00:45.379
Okay.

00:45.463 --> 00:47.089
CHAPTER 12: YOU GUYS WANT TO GO OUT
INTO THE REAL WORLD, RIGHT?

00:55.097 --> 00:56.766
Oh, hello, sir.

00:56.849 --> 00:59.268
-Eui-ju! Are you still here?
-Yes.

00:59.351 --> 01:01.729
I'm going to drop by the library.

01:03.147 --> 01:04.315
Is something bothering you?

01:07.943 --> 01:09.361
I think

01:09.445 --> 01:11.822
my homeroom teacher has it in for me.

01:13.157 --> 01:14.325
Why?

01:15.159 --> 01:18.078
Ever since that misunderstanding
about the filming,

01:18.162 --> 01:20.039
he's been acting like he hates me.

01:21.624 --> 01:22.500
No way.

01:23.459 --> 01:24.668
It's true.

01:24.752 --> 01:28.130
First, he embarrassed me in front
of everyone by asking me my math score.

01:28.214 --> 01:31.300
Then he made me write an apology
because I said I hated math.

01:31.383 --> 01:34.011
And now he's giving me demerits
for a ridiculous reason.

01:35.554 --> 01:37.723
He wouldn't do that for no reason.

01:44.063 --> 01:45.064
Goodbye.

01:45.773 --> 01:47.983
See you tomorrow.

01:53.948 --> 01:55.199
Hey, Yoon!

01:55.282 --> 01:57.451
I thought you wanted
to take Discrete Math together.

01:58.911 --> 02:00.496
No, no, no.

02:03.833 --> 02:06.085
This ending is lame.

02:06.168 --> 02:10.130
Tae-ha can't let Si-on just walk away.

02:10.214 --> 02:11.173
The math…

02:12.132 --> 02:12.967
I mean,

02:13.676 --> 02:14.552
Ju Si-on.

02:15.302 --> 02:17.096
You deserve a beating.

02:18.389 --> 02:19.598
It's going to hurt.

02:19.682 --> 02:22.560
Blame it on the personality
of the person you're based on.

02:26.772 --> 02:27.690
Good.

02:29.859 --> 02:31.443
HIS EYES BLAZE WITH OBSESSION…

02:33.779 --> 02:34.655
Hey, Ju Si-on!

02:39.952 --> 02:41.120
TAE-HA PUNCHES SI-ON

02:50.713 --> 02:52.298
-Let's go.
-You're bleeding.

02:52.381 --> 02:53.799
-I'm fine.
-Hang on a second.

02:54.800 --> 02:56.552
One punch just isn't enough. Do it again.

02:56.635 --> 02:58.012
Sorry?

03:00.306 --> 03:01.181
-Again?
-One more?

03:02.474 --> 03:03.934
Just a moment!

03:12.026 --> 03:12.985
There we go.

03:13.068 --> 03:14.737
That hits the spot.

03:16.405 --> 03:17.323
That's better!

03:23.078 --> 03:24.121
This is really great.

03:24.204 --> 03:27.583
How can I keep it to myself?

03:31.086 --> 03:32.296
Shall I just upload it?

03:36.175 --> 03:37.009
Right?

03:37.968 --> 03:41.013
You guys want to go out
into the real world, right?

03:43.140 --> 03:44.725
If I'm this excited,

03:44.808 --> 03:47.561
you guys must be even more so.

03:48.687 --> 03:51.774
-Do it!
-Do it!

03:51.857 --> 03:54.151
-Do it!
-Do it!

03:54.234 --> 03:56.028
-Do it!
-Do it!

03:56.111 --> 03:57.529
Shall I just upload it?

04:11.293 --> 04:12.878
Nobody's going to find out.

04:23.472 --> 04:24.598
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

04:29.770 --> 04:32.773
-We're going out into the real world!
-We're going out into the real world!

04:32.856 --> 04:34.316
WE WERE FRIENDS

04:41.907 --> 04:45.619
CHAPTER 13: ARE HIS GLASSES
REALLY THAT BIG A DEAL?

04:51.458 --> 04:53.627
EPISODE 4

04:55.295 --> 04:56.130
Is it that bad?

04:59.717 --> 05:00.634
I'll be okay.

05:01.218 --> 05:03.470
Why would someone take glasses
they can't even use?

05:05.305 --> 05:06.390
That's it!

05:08.392 --> 05:09.476
Up in a tree.

05:09.560 --> 05:11.061
You said you threw them.

05:11.145 --> 05:13.188
If they're not on the ground,
they must be in a tree.

05:14.189 --> 05:16.108
I thought of that,
so I looked on the way home.

05:16.191 --> 05:17.026
They weren't there.

05:18.694 --> 05:19.945
So where have they gotten to?

05:20.863 --> 05:22.865
Did a pigeon take them to build its nest?

05:24.074 --> 05:25.159
Yes!

05:25.242 --> 05:27.911
They do say that magpies and such
like shiny things.

05:27.995 --> 05:30.956
Apparently, sometimes they take them
to decorate their nests.

05:32.916 --> 05:34.251
Just get some new ones.

05:34.334 --> 05:37.755
The problem is it's not that
straightforward to make new ones.

05:40.132 --> 05:41.300
Are you done?

05:42.551 --> 05:43.677
He's hardly eaten anything.

05:45.304 --> 05:46.388
They're in a nest.

06:19.046 --> 06:19.963
What's wrong with him?

06:23.717 --> 06:24.843
I think he's really sick.

06:28.931 --> 06:30.516
I think I need to take a sick day.

06:31.141 --> 06:33.310
Okay, I'll let them know at school.

06:34.103 --> 06:35.145
Get some rest.

06:36.480 --> 06:38.816
Laid low by a pair of glasses.

06:59.962 --> 07:01.630
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

07:17.229 --> 07:19.398
Mr. Ga is feeling unwell,

07:19.481 --> 07:21.859
so I'll be taking homeroom today.

07:21.942 --> 07:23.277
Let's start with roll call.

07:24.027 --> 07:25.362
-Kim Ga-yeong.
-Here!

07:26.530 --> 07:27.489
Kim Dan-ji.

07:28.365 --> 07:30.242
-Here!
-Kim Yeong-jae.

07:30.325 --> 07:31.410
Here.

07:31.493 --> 07:33.078
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

07:33.162 --> 07:34.371
I hope our teacher changes.

07:34.454 --> 07:36.790
-Choi Yu-mi.
-It'd be amazing if it was Dong-ju.

07:36.874 --> 07:38.500
-Right?
-Yeah.

07:39.168 --> 07:40.586
-Jeon Ji-min.
-Here.

07:42.921 --> 07:45.799
He looked fine yesterday.

07:46.550 --> 07:48.760
Maybe he bunked off
to hang out with his girlfriend.

07:48.844 --> 07:51.346
That would be amazing.

07:51.430 --> 07:54.975
He's being punished
for being mean to Eui-ju.

07:55.058 --> 07:57.227
Giving my girl demerits for no reason.

07:57.311 --> 07:58.854
-Right?
-Yeah.

08:00.355 --> 08:01.231
Cute.

08:03.609 --> 08:05.736
-Jenny, do you ever diet?
-Why?

08:08.780 --> 08:10.824
Hello, Mr. Ga. Are you okay?

08:13.035 --> 08:15.746
Oh, no! Please take good care of yourself.

08:16.580 --> 08:18.373
Don't worry about us.

08:19.875 --> 08:22.586
I'll make sure to tell the others
in homeroom.

08:23.921 --> 08:26.340
Okay. Get some rest.

08:42.564 --> 08:45.025
I explained
the concept of Rolle's Theorem.

08:45.108 --> 08:48.487
If we insert one here…

08:50.364 --> 08:53.075
And if we insert five here…

08:56.578 --> 08:57.621
Great work.

08:57.704 --> 08:59.873
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

08:59.957 --> 09:01.291
We're done.

09:01.375 --> 09:02.251
I'm so sleepy.

09:02.876 --> 09:04.878
I'm so sleepy.

09:05.587 --> 09:07.089
Guys, can I have your attention?

09:07.172 --> 09:09.341
Is Mr. Ga not coming to school
tomorrow either?

09:11.051 --> 09:14.513
Applications for after-school programs
are due by tomorrow so don't forget.

09:15.472 --> 09:16.306
That's all.

09:18.558 --> 09:21.645
-Did she just ignore me?
-Yeah.

09:21.728 --> 09:22.938
I'm off to art academy.

09:23.730 --> 09:24.564
Bye.

09:29.486 --> 09:31.321
Is he really sick?

09:33.740 --> 09:34.825
It's none of my business.

09:39.997 --> 09:42.874
MISSING GLASSES

09:42.958 --> 09:45.085
At this rate, he'll have
to take a leave of absence.

09:47.045 --> 09:48.088
What did the doctor say?

09:48.171 --> 09:50.048
He has to keep resting.

09:50.132 --> 09:52.175
If he overdoes it,
he risks damaging his other eye.

09:53.218 --> 09:54.594
Oh, hello.

09:55.178 --> 09:56.471
Is that your application form?

09:57.597 --> 10:00.309
What's up with Mr. Ga's glasses?

10:01.977 --> 10:02.894
The thing is…

10:05.230 --> 10:06.523
MISSING GLASSES

10:07.316 --> 10:10.485
Are his glasses really that big a deal?

10:14.364 --> 10:16.199
They're special glasses.

10:17.409 --> 10:19.411
He was trying to soldier on,
but in the end…

10:20.746 --> 10:22.831
It's going to take a long time
to make new ones.

10:22.914 --> 10:24.041
I'm quite worried.

10:34.926 --> 10:36.803
Oh! No!

10:41.516 --> 10:43.101
Hey!

10:43.185 --> 10:45.062
Ga-yun!

10:45.145 --> 10:47.356
-Stop!
-What is it?

10:47.439 --> 10:49.191
Let me borrow your bike for a bit.

10:49.274 --> 10:51.234
-My bike?
-I'll give it back later. Quickly!

10:51.318 --> 10:52.736
-Sure.
-Quick!

10:52.819 --> 10:53.779
Thank you.

10:59.868 --> 11:01.495
Move out the way.

11:01.578 --> 11:02.704
Hey!

11:17.761 --> 11:19.304
Hey!

11:20.055 --> 11:21.264
Hey!

11:22.724 --> 11:23.975
Come on!

11:32.442 --> 11:33.652
Wait!

11:33.735 --> 11:35.237
No!

11:36.363 --> 11:37.948
Come on!

11:38.031 --> 11:38.990
Wait!

11:43.578 --> 11:44.830
Stop!

11:44.913 --> 11:46.373
Hey! Please!

11:51.545 --> 11:53.088
Hey!

11:57.008 --> 11:58.051
Hey!

12:07.477 --> 12:08.478
Hey!

12:12.149 --> 12:13.775
Please!

12:13.859 --> 12:16.528
How far are you going?

12:18.405 --> 12:20.198
Please stop!

12:23.410 --> 12:24.995
Mister!

12:35.714 --> 12:38.341
What the hell are you doing?
It's dangerous!

12:38.425 --> 12:39.718
I'm sorry.

12:39.801 --> 12:41.052
But…

12:41.136 --> 12:43.054
You've got to help me.

12:43.138 --> 12:45.307
My teacher's going to die without them.

12:46.016 --> 12:47.601
What are you talking about?

12:48.351 --> 12:49.519
The thing is…

12:50.645 --> 12:54.065
I threw my teacher's glasses in the trash.

12:54.149 --> 12:56.485
But without them, he's going to die.

12:58.487 --> 13:00.280
Can you help me out?

13:00.363 --> 13:02.574
Please. They're in there.

13:04.326 --> 13:06.536
Please…

13:09.039 --> 13:11.917
MUNICIPAL DUMP

13:12.000 --> 13:13.543
Are you sure they're in here?

13:13.627 --> 13:16.713
Yes, I threw them out yesterday.

13:18.006 --> 13:19.883
Why would you do that?

13:20.550 --> 13:22.052
I know.

13:23.094 --> 13:24.471
And why look for them again?

13:25.347 --> 13:26.640
I know.

13:27.933 --> 13:29.476
I'm really sorry.

13:29.559 --> 13:30.685
I'll be as quick as I can.

13:37.609 --> 13:38.777
Mister.

13:38.860 --> 13:40.403
I'm really grateful.

13:40.487 --> 13:41.404
I'll search.

13:41.488 --> 13:43.740
I'll be really quick
and clear it all up again.

13:58.964 --> 14:00.090
Oh, look.

14:00.173 --> 14:01.466
I've found them.

14:01.550 --> 14:02.551
Is that them?

14:03.552 --> 14:04.844
These are the ones.

14:11.351 --> 14:13.311
Thank you.

14:13.395 --> 14:14.437
Thank you so much.

14:14.521 --> 14:18.567
CHAPTER 14: YOU BREAKING MY GLASSES CAUSED
TEN MILLION WON'S WORTH OF DAMAGE

14:24.489 --> 14:25.448
Where did you find them?

14:27.450 --> 14:29.160
They were on the bench with poop on it.

14:29.244 --> 14:30.662
They were already broken.

14:35.959 --> 14:37.002
4073.

14:41.214 --> 14:43.091
That's the last four digits
of your phone number.

14:46.011 --> 14:49.264
One of my students has the same number.

14:54.311 --> 14:56.104
YEO EUI-JU

14:56.646 --> 14:57.564
What's your name?

15:00.108 --> 15:01.651
Why is that important?

15:01.735 --> 15:04.237
Just give me the money.
I have to go to PC room.

15:04.779 --> 15:05.655
Name.

15:06.239 --> 15:07.407
Yeo Eui-do.

15:11.620 --> 15:12.621
Call your sister.

15:13.371 --> 15:14.372
Why?

15:15.206 --> 15:16.041
Just do it.

15:28.803 --> 15:31.056
Hi, what is it?

15:31.139 --> 15:32.849
There's someone who wants to talk to you.

15:38.313 --> 15:39.189
Yeo Eui-ju.

15:48.865 --> 15:50.659
You stole your teacher's glasses?

15:50.742 --> 15:51.785
You're nuts.

15:53.578 --> 15:54.996
Now she's here, you can go.

15:56.247 --> 15:57.582
And talk to her nicely.

16:08.677 --> 16:09.636
Sir.

16:11.054 --> 16:13.723
So what happened was…

16:13.807 --> 16:17.018
I clearly asked
if you'd stepped on my glasses.

16:18.478 --> 16:21.856
You could have said something when we were
all looking, or again in the parking lot.

16:24.651 --> 16:27.362
But you looked me right in the eye
and said it wasn't you.

16:28.780 --> 16:29.656
I…

16:30.657 --> 16:31.574
I was scared…

16:32.701 --> 16:35.870
I'd get in trouble for breaking them.

16:37.372 --> 16:38.998
But…

16:39.082 --> 16:41.626
You gave me four demerits because of Ji-a.

16:41.710 --> 16:44.003
I don't think I did anything wrong.

16:44.671 --> 16:46.464
It seemed so unfair.

16:47.048 --> 16:50.009
And I feel like you hate me.

16:53.012 --> 16:54.723
I was wrong.

16:56.766 --> 16:59.519
I didn't know they were special glasses.

16:59.602 --> 17:01.563
If I knew your eyes were so bad,

17:01.646 --> 17:03.648
I'd have given them back to you
straightaway.

17:05.400 --> 17:07.068
I shouldn't have done what I did.

17:07.861 --> 17:09.821
I'm truly sorry.

17:34.721 --> 17:35.597
So.

17:36.723 --> 17:38.850
It was clearly your fault
and you've admitted it.

17:39.476 --> 17:40.935
All that's left is compensation.

17:41.728 --> 17:42.729
Compensation?

17:44.022 --> 17:46.941
You breaking my glasses caused
ten million won's worth of damage.

17:47.650 --> 17:49.152
Ten million won?

17:49.235 --> 17:51.070
What kind of glasses cost ten million won?

17:52.155 --> 17:54.157
I can't take money from a student.

17:54.240 --> 17:56.326
So you'll have to find another way
to repay me.

17:57.368 --> 17:58.203
Okay.

17:58.828 --> 18:00.330
I will.

18:00.413 --> 18:02.582
However I can. Whatever it takes.

18:03.374 --> 18:04.834
I'll give you one chance.

18:07.045 --> 18:08.463
Thank you, sir.

18:08.546 --> 18:10.006
I'll do anything.

18:10.882 --> 18:11.841
After-school math.

18:13.426 --> 18:14.302
Sorry?

18:14.385 --> 18:16.054
I'm going to give you the chance

18:16.137 --> 18:18.640
to rediscover your passion for math
and improve your grades.

18:20.517 --> 18:21.935
What's the point?

18:23.228 --> 18:26.439
Sir, that class is only for smart kids.

18:26.523 --> 18:27.899
The ones who are top of the class.

18:28.650 --> 18:31.820
Before class,
set the temperature to 23 degrees,

18:31.903 --> 18:34.447
put the handouts on the desks,

18:34.531 --> 18:35.657
and collect any homework.

18:35.740 --> 18:38.952
After class, clean up,
put everything away, and lock the door.

18:39.577 --> 18:40.787
I really can't.

18:44.624 --> 18:45.667
Wednesday at five.

18:46.459 --> 18:47.627
Wednesday at five?

18:48.753 --> 18:51.965
Sir, I'm supposed to do after-school PE
at that time.

18:52.048 --> 18:54.092
I really can't do Wednesday at five.

18:58.471 --> 18:59.472
Don't forget.

19:02.141 --> 19:03.268
Ten million won.

19:14.195 --> 19:16.072
I really can't.

19:18.116 --> 19:19.492
What am I going to do?

19:35.216 --> 19:37.176
What?

19:37.260 --> 19:38.177
My reward.

19:38.803 --> 19:40.138
I didn't get it because of you.

19:40.221 --> 19:41.556
Hey!

19:41.639 --> 19:44.809
What money do I have?
I already spent my allowance.

19:46.728 --> 19:48.229
-Mom!
-Wait!

19:49.188 --> 19:50.231
Okay.

19:56.571 --> 19:58.031
This is all I have.

19:59.532 --> 20:00.992
You should learn to budget.

20:10.126 --> 20:12.837
Why of all people did it have to be him
to get dirt on me?

20:12.921 --> 20:14.005
So annoying!

20:14.797 --> 20:16.591
So annoying!

20:21.429 --> 20:22.263
Hang on.

20:22.347 --> 20:24.432
It's clearly your fault
and you've admitted it.

20:25.058 --> 20:26.476
All that's left is compensation.

20:26.935 --> 20:28.895
Don't forget. Ten million won.

20:29.604 --> 20:32.523
He does come up with
a lot of really great dialogue.

20:43.201 --> 20:45.328
I bet mine's been buried way down again.

20:54.629 --> 20:55.672
WEB NOVEL RANKING

20:55.755 --> 20:56.923
Number one?

20:59.050 --> 21:00.259
Hang on a second.

21:00.343 --> 21:03.096
1. WE WERE FRIENDS
VIEWS: 130K

21:05.848 --> 21:07.600
WE WERE FRIENDS

21:07.684 --> 21:08.768
What the heck?

21:10.061 --> 21:11.145
How many favorites?

21:12.313 --> 21:13.982
One, ten,

21:14.732 --> 21:16.401
hundred…

21:16.484 --> 21:17.527
FAVORITES 15,320

21:17.610 --> 21:19.445
15,320?

21:21.280 --> 21:22.156
What's going on?

21:23.241 --> 21:25.076
Is this definitely mine?

21:27.954 --> 21:29.038
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 1

21:33.167 --> 21:36.421
I'm from the future.
This novel is going to be huge.

21:36.504 --> 21:38.172
Please let Yoon and Si-on end up together.

21:38.256 --> 21:39.757
Tae-ha's in true love.

21:39.841 --> 21:41.384
Really looking forward to their story.

21:41.467 --> 21:42.301
What the heck?

21:45.847 --> 21:46.889
That hurt!

21:49.434 --> 21:50.351
Then…

21:51.060 --> 21:52.061
is this real?

21:52.145 --> 21:53.271
It's real?

21:57.900 --> 21:59.569
The tension is thick right from the off.

21:59.652 --> 22:02.405
-You could cut it with a knife.
-Tae-ha, you had me at red bean bread.

22:02.488 --> 22:04.282
Yoon is so much more complicated
than math.

22:04.365 --> 22:06.034
This line alone
tells the outlook of this story.

22:11.164 --> 22:12.832
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 2

22:16.753 --> 22:18.129
WHAT? AM I TOO CLOSE?
YOON SHOOK…

22:24.385 --> 22:25.970
Dan-ji found Mr. Noh's Instagram.

22:26.054 --> 22:28.097
I found photos of him
from back in college.

22:28.181 --> 22:29.182
Amazing!

22:29.265 --> 22:30.767
Can you try looking for Dong-ju's?

22:30.850 --> 22:32.643
How much are you going to pay me?

22:32.727 --> 22:33.936
Get lost.

22:34.020 --> 22:36.105
Why is Eui-ju so quiet?

22:36.189 --> 22:37.857
Is she actually studying?

22:39.192 --> 22:42.737
YOON SHOOK HIS HEAD BUT…

22:54.832 --> 22:55.666
You're late.

22:57.668 --> 22:58.753
I'm tired.

23:00.213 --> 23:01.047
We need to talk.

23:01.839 --> 23:02.840
I have nothing to say.

23:02.924 --> 23:05.051
If I say we talk, we talk, got it?

23:05.134 --> 23:06.677
-I said I have nothing…
-Shut up!

23:06.761 --> 23:07.595
Let go of me!

23:13.893 --> 23:14.769
Sorry.

23:15.269 --> 23:17.480
I told you to let go of me.

23:17.563 --> 23:18.898
Are you okay?

23:21.109 --> 23:23.277
It was clearly your fault
and you've admitted it.

23:25.029 --> 23:26.614
All that's left is compensation.

23:28.407 --> 23:29.367
Compensation?

23:34.622 --> 23:35.456
Ten million won.

23:37.333 --> 23:38.501
What?

23:38.584 --> 23:41.170
You splitting my lip caused
ten million won's worth of damage.

23:41.838 --> 23:43.506
What do you mean ten million won?

23:43.589 --> 23:45.508
Heard of a little thing
called "scarcity value"?

23:45.591 --> 23:47.718
The rarer something is,
the more valuable it becomes.

23:47.802 --> 23:49.762
Because people want it even more.

23:51.222 --> 23:53.641
Just like my lips,
which I don't just allow anyone to have.

23:56.853 --> 23:59.897
You're poor, so instead of money, you'll
have to find another way to repay me.

24:03.818 --> 24:05.069
Wednesday at five.

24:05.903 --> 24:06.863
Come to my place.

24:08.156 --> 24:09.740
Don't be even one second late.

24:15.454 --> 24:16.497
That ten million won.

24:21.627 --> 24:23.171
Pay me back properly.

24:48.446 --> 24:50.698
You're not treating her like that
on purpose, are you?

24:50.781 --> 24:52.825
Why are you being so strict with just her?

24:52.909 --> 24:55.995
Blink twice if you're here under duress.

24:56.078 --> 24:59.790
I can't accept her
only getting four points in math.

25:00.666 --> 25:02.376
You keep making me think bad thoughts.

25:02.460 --> 25:03.294
Yeo Eui-ju.

25:03.377 --> 25:05.254
I didn't realize
you were such a lost cause.

25:05.338 --> 25:06.297
I'm very disappointed.

25:06.380 --> 25:08.549
Is Tae-ha gonna be waiting
outside your house again?

25:08.633 --> 25:09.967
I don't know. Stop messing around.

25:10.843 --> 25:11.719
What's so funny?

25:11.802 --> 25:12.678
Is it R-rated?

25:13.179 --> 25:14.722
It's not like BL, is it?

25:14.805 --> 25:17.433
Now that's a proper cliffhanger.

25:17.516 --> 25:20.019
There's no way
you can skip the next episode.

26:16.575 --> 26:18.577
Subtitle: Paul Carver
